73
00:03:09,913 --> 00:03:12,270
If you go there and you need something,

74
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,853
you need a new driver's license or anything

75
00:03:14,885 --> 00:03:15,286
like that,

76
00:03:15,847 --> 00:03:18,494
they need to be able to quickly find your

77
00:03:18,494 --> 00:03:18,975
record.

78
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,894
And it's easy to find it if you give them

79
00:03:22,247 --> 00:03:24,637
your ID, your name, your address, whatever

80
00:03:24,653 --> 00:03:26,770
was used as a key to store your data.

81
00:03:27,315 --> 00:03:29,433
In that case, they can quickly look up your

82
00:03:29,481 --> 00:03:32,031
data and find all the other data they might

83
00:03:32,031 --> 00:03:34,132
need to give you a new driver's license.

84
00:03:34,838 --> 00:03:37,789
If the data would only be stored as a list,

85
00:03:37,950 --> 00:03:40,114
So if we just had record after record

86
00:03:40,146 --> 00:03:42,454
without any key, they would have to go

87
00:03:42,775 --> 00:03:45,356
through all the records of all the

88
00:03:45,356 --> 00:03:46,526
inhabitants in the city.

89
00:03:47,103 --> 00:03:49,347
And as you can imagine, that would be a lot

90
00:03:49,427 --> 00:03:49,796
of work.

91
00:03:50,325 --> 00:03:52,874
That's why in such a scenario, tables are

92
00:03:52,874 --> 00:03:53,147
better.

